{
  "id": "book-34",
  "checkpoint": 18,
  "title": "Reaching the Summit Marker",
  "summary": "Paul e Clara superam os últimos metros da subida, chegam ao marco de pedra no cume da montanha e celebram a conquista com uma vista infinita.",
  "audio_url": "/audios/book-34.mp3",
  "word_count_target": 140,
  "story_en": "The final stretch of the trail requires steady hands and patient steps. Paul and Clara climb past the last towering boulder. Suddenly, the steep ground levels out into a wide stone plateau.\n\nIn the exact center stands the historical summit marker, built from carved granite. An ancient metal plate confirms the altitude of North Peak.\n\nPaul unslings his heavy pack and stands beside Clara. A 360-degree panorama unfolds around them. Drifting white clouds float below their feet, while distant mountain chains stretch endlessly beneath a crystal-clear blue sky.\n\n“We made it to the top,” Clara says, raising her arms in pure celebration.\n\n“Every step was worth the effort,” Paul replies, feeling an overwhelming sense of accomplishment. He writes his name in the summit guestbook, marking the completion of this unforgettable climb.",
